{
  "_readme": [
    "Tamil Nadu districts with their headquarters coordinates, in WGS84.",
    "",
    "Shared reference data: the GRIB pipeline (ml/grib_to_csv.py) maps each district",
    "to its nearest ERA5 grid node, and the backend resolves a district name to a",
    "location for scoring. Defined once here so the two cannot drift apart.",
    "",
    "COORDINATES are the district headquarters town, not the district centroid. For a",
    "0.25 degree (~27 km) climate grid the difference is well inside one cell, so the",
    "nearest-node lookup lands on the same cell either way.",
    "",
    "COVERAGE: the bundled data.grib spans 8-15 N, 75-80 E. Districts east of 80 E -",
    "notably Chennai at 80.27 E - fall OUTSIDE that grid. They are listed here anyway",
    "because the list describes Tamil Nadu, not one particular data file; the pipeline",
    "reports which districts it could and could not cover rather than silently",
    "dropping them.",
    "",
    "PRIORITY districts named in the build spec are flagged so the pipeline can report",
    "on them explicitly."
  ],
